Package: argitect
Type: Package
Title: Native Command-Line Argument Parsing with Rich Help Messages
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("argitect", "authors", email = "argitect@example.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A pure-R command-line argument parser that reimplements the
    functionality of the Perl module Getopt::Long without any external
    dependency, and additionally supports positional arguments. It provides
    rich, customizable help messages inspired by the 'GetoptLong' package,
    including one-column and two-column styles, template-based usage text,
    option grouping, default-value reporting and sub-option documentation,
    as well as sub-command dispatch. 
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: methods, GlobalOptions (>= 0.1.0)
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
NeedsCompilation: no
Collate:
    'argitect-package.R'
    '0_global.R'
    'opt_utils.R'
    'SingleArgument-class.R'
    'argitect.R'
    'print.R'
    'sub_commands.R'
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
